<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>France 24 - International breaking news, top stories and headlines</title><subtitle type="html">Breaking news and world news from France 24 on Business, Sports, Culture. Video news. News from the US, Europe, Asia Pacific, Africa, Middle East, America</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/rss</id><updated>2026-10-06T06:35:25Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Nations League: France defeat Belgium in second-half comeback</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ab7b5a1055bd75e14ce42fcea7ee98c0313ea8a630ff1d06506b736e54ad7413</id><updated>2026-10-06T06:34:31Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T06:28:17Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/sports/20261006-nations-league-france-defeat-belgium-in-second-half-comeback--e6be834a8f9d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/sports/20261006-nations-league-france-defeat-belgium-in-second-half-comeback" /><summary type="html">Despite being behind at halftime, France scored four goals in 15 minutes to defeat Belgium (4-1). Thanks to this win, France are first in Group 1 after four matches.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Ukraine hits Moscow with one of its largest drone attacks in two years</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3f659affa682b9f843fde429ab298a0c41eb9d4d606f80b709bc64c19579710d</id><updated>2026-10-06T06:34:34Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T06:11:43Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261006-massive-ukrainian-drone-attack-targets-moscow-russian-officials-say--d7ae0a7240b4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261006-massive-ukrainian-drone-attack-targets-moscow-russian-officials-say" /><summary type="html">Ukraine launched overnight one of its largest drone attacks on Moscow in the past two years, killing one man and injuring several people in the Russian capital, local officials said on Tuesday.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Trump targets tax-free diesel as Republicans approach midterms</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:207a1d49c34a2087ddc7b0907d4de905536ec715c857d0cfd823420fe46e4053</id><updated>2026-10-06T06:34:37Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T03:08:02Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261006-trump-targets-tax-free-diesel-as-republicans-approach-midterms--32be17b93388.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261006-trump-targets-tax-free-diesel-as-republicans-approach-midterms" /><summary type="html">President Donald Trump on Monday signed an executive order to ease limits on tax-free red-dyed diesel as fuel prices put pressure on Republican candidates. Trump said the move would save farmers millions of dollars and lower the cost of goods, though analysts said the change would not benefit farmers already using tax-exempt fuel.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Live: Tens of thousands expected at Paris protests as unions join students</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fe09e8fd4ffdb6e92db496618e1c45a8e4d4856aae5b2e2f6d4b7a02c84a144d</id><updated>2026-10-06T06:34:40Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T02:31:54Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261006-live-tens-of-thousands-expected-at-paris-protests-as-unions-join-students--df93e10e4e3b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261006-live-tens-of-thousands-expected-at-paris-protests-as-unions-join-students" /><summary type="html">Up to 40,000 people are expected to march in Paris on Tuesday as French trade unions join high school students protesting school conditions. The demonstrations have been marked by clashes with police, arrests, and injuries, including a 15-year-old student whose hand was blown off after he picked up a ‌police grenade. Follow our liveblog for the latest updates.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Trump approves firing-squad execution of Fort Hood shooter Nidal Hasan</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a071de06c162b3d96cb895eae056e20ab6fb57aa1ba5f553b514ebd7602fa412</id><updated>2026-10-06T06:34:43Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T01:31:37Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261006-trump-approves-firing-squad-execution-of-fort-hood-shooter-nidal-hasan--e67cc0cf0a56.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261006-trump-approves-firing-squad-execution-of-fort-hood-shooter-nidal-hasan" /><summary type="html">President Donald Trump approved a firing squad execution on Monday for Nidal Hasan, the US Army psychiatrist convicted of killing 13 people at Fort Hood in 2009. Hasan's execution will be the first carried out by the US military since 1961, with the date and location yet to be set by the Army.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Switching on brain cells: the Nobel-winning science of optogenetics</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:875d2dd5106be8cb9664547730847fd0a0abaaa3559d54dd09fcad55e51f3d54</id><updated>2026-10-06T06:34:46Z</updated><published>2026-10-05T21:56:30Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/switching-on-brain-cells-the-nobel-winning-science-of-optogenetics--59805e2fcba1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/switching-on-brain-cells-the-nobel-winning-science-of-optogenetics" /><summary type="html">The Nobel medicine prize was awarded Monday to US psychiatrist and neurologist Karl Deisseroth and German scientists Peter Hegemann and Georg Nagel for their pioneering work in the neuroscience field of optogenetics. In optogenetics, scientists control neurones by stimulating them with light -- potentially unlocking breakthroughs for conditions such as dementia, depression and blindness. FRANCE 24's Monte Francis reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>Quebec votes as separatist surge poses test for Canada PM</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:916fa4bd9d2f8d91c6a907d7a9921e28751c57b58921729208778389f304860c</id><updated>2026-10-06T06:34:49Z</updated><published>2026-10-05T21:36:57Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/quebec-votes-as-separatist-surge-poses-test-for-canada-pm--438982eb3074.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/quebec-votes-as-separatist-surge-poses-test-for-canada-pm" /><summary type="html">Quebec separatists eyed a return to power in Canada's majority French-speaking province Monday in an election that could test Prime Minister Mark Carney's message of national unity to confront the United States. Carney is popular in Quebec, and the possible success of the separatist Parti Quebecois (PQ) is not seen as a repudiation of his stance toward President Donald Trump, whose trade war and annexation threats have infuriated Canadians. FRANCE 24's Christopher Guly reports from Ottawa.</summary></entry><entry><title>New York declares statewide disaster emergency as measles cases rise</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fbd87fe17c329e3dbf6fb053a6345918ea4de695c55e643667ba13caf860c1bd</id><updated>2026-10-06T06:34:52Z</updated><published>2026-10-05T21:23:04Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261005-new-york-declares-statewide-disaster-emergency-as-measles-cases-rise--535ca35f113f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261005-new-york-declares-statewide-disaster-emergency-as-measles-cases-rise" /><summary type="html">New York Governor Kathy Hochul declared a statewide disaster emergency on Monday as a measles outbreak spreads through under-immunised rural communities, with 108 cases reported this year. The order expands who can administer MMR vaccines and comes as neighbouring Pennsylvania battles an outbreak that has killed five people.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Euro falls to 17-month low against the USD on French debt concerns</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a78dcef97e60f2b0f2275d3615369d81987d7e3f7da5cd8139e76aebdb9defd1</id><updated>2026-10-06T06:34:55Z</updated><published>2026-10-05T20:51:22Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/business/20261005-euro-falls-to-17-month-low-against-the-usd-on-french-debt-concerns--522517cf756b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/business/20261005-euro-falls-to-17-month-low-against-the-usd-on-french-debt-concerns" /><summary type="html">The euro has stumbled to a 17-month low against the US dollar on concern about France's ability to bring its public finances in order.  The currency has fallen nearly 7% from its peak in late January.  Meanwhile, global oil prices fell despite ongoing tensions around the Arabian Peninsula, after the G7 agreed to release up to 100 million barrels from strategic reserves and oil flows from the Persian Gulf have returned to pre-war levels.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Concerns of US interference weigh on Brazil vote</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:18576a30566cbc1e212d8a600ba6efddd308aef6d7746e412dc2ef1a6359aae6</id><updated>2026-10-06T06:34:58Z</updated><published>2026-10-05T20:37:01Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/concerns-of-us-interference-weigh-on-brazil-vote--868141281be7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/concerns-of-us-interference-weigh-on-brazil-vote" /><summary type="html">Conservative Senator Flavio Bolsonaro pulled off a surprise on Sunday in the first round of Brazil’s presidential election by finishing ahead of the incumbent left-wing President Lula, whom he will face in the runoff on October 25. Suspicions of U.S. interference have been hanging over the campaign, even as Donald Trump has never hidden his closeness to the far-right former president Bolsonaro - Flavio’s father - and his animosity toward Lula da Silva. FRANCE 24's Emerald Maxwell reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>Ethiopia again demands access to the Red Sea</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0dd7a000331b6a433ea352127d45ce4490aef403594fa587e5cc09d5525e1e1a</id><updated>2026-10-06T06:35:01Z</updated><published>2026-10-05T20:28:19Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/ethiopia-again-demands-access-to-the-red-sea--806dbf10a5ba.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/ethiopia-again-demands-access-to-the-red-sea" /><summary type="html">In tonight's edition, Ethiopia's leader Abiy Ahmed secures another term, but his country is sliding back into conflict. Also, several major cities across Senegal are battered by torrential rains. And some of the migrants being deported from the US fear the return to countries criminalizing homosexuality.</summary><category term="Eye on Africa" /></entry><entry><title>Indian alleged mastermind of online child abuse ring goes on trial in Paris</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:93e88de2c6cae4308affc2839a08ece911e62c0f92d7cd9797ad1a10a5820790</id><updated>2026-10-06T06:35:04Z</updated><published>2026-10-05T20:15:18Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/france/20261005-indian-alleged-mastermind-of-online-child-abuse-ring-goes-on-trial-in-paris--91d91c8213a3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/france/20261005-indian-alleged-mastermind-of-online-child-abuse-ring-goes-on-trial-in-paris" /><summary type="html">Rohan Rane, an Indian national who came to France to study before becoming a fitness coach, went on trial on Monday behind closed doors in Paris, on charges of torture and acts of barbarity against minors. Investigators say he is the leader of a neo-Nazi child exploitation ring that ran its operations via messaging platform Discord.</summary><category term="France" /></entry><entry><title>‘France has fallen’: Far-right figures fuel Islamophobic claims with false student protest videos</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9669add27d7c116db24dc2fd96dfb343d5b27ef663e56872b6aeaa1fb1d4e37f</id><updated>2026-10-06T06:35:07Z</updated><published>2026-10-05T20:10:15Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/france-has-fallen-far-right-figures-fuel-islamophobic-claims-with-false-student-protest-videos-1--01d2303272c5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/france-has-fallen-far-right-figures-fuel-islamophobic-claims-with-false-student-protest-videos-1" /><summary type="html">France’s student protests have become the target of a wave of false and misleading videos shared by far-right figures, including Alex Jones and Tommy Robinson. Old footage and unrelated videos have been shared to portray the demonstrations as evidence of an “anti-white” or Islamist uprising linked to uncontrolled immigration. The protests are over school conditions, including large class sizes, teacher shortages and poor facilities, not immigration. Vedika Bahl fact-checks in Truth or Fake.</summary><category term="Truth or Fake" /></entry><entry><title>'We are effectively maiming young people' - expert questions France's response to student protests</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:00b1ed57400c96c97e548a9cb21ba3fe185b134d6ed479bda41b550a4a34afe4</id><updated>2026-10-06T06:35:10Z</updated><published>2026-10-05T20:08:48Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/we-are-effectively-maiming-young-people-expert-questions-france-s-response-to-student-protests--524561dc9727.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/we-are-effectively-maiming-young-people-expert-questions-france-s-response-to-student-protests" /><summary type="html">A 15-year-old lost a hand on Monday picking up a police grenade amid nationwide school protests demanding better funding and classroom conditions. Speaking with FRANCE 24's Mark Owen, Ariane Bogain, Senior Lecturer in French Politics at Northumbria University, says that "there is a definite issue with violence and we need to ask why there is this unidimensional reaction which is aggressive, which is riot police, which is repressive".</summary></entry><entry><title>Sanchez chose 'best moment in a sea of troubles' to call for snap election, analyst says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4f966ed9590fe4d50e1813fd0024f1232f1cb1170aaa4179757c7da2d8d5e390</id><updated>2026-10-06T06:35:14Z</updated><published>2026-10-05T19:31:33Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/sanchez-chose-best-moment-in-a-sea-of-troubles-to-call-for-snap-election-analyst-says--d3b32568f53b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/sanchez-chose-best-moment-in-a-sea-of-troubles-to-call-for-snap-election-analyst-says" /><summary type="html">Spanish Prime Minister Pedro Sanchez on Monday called an early election for November 29, aiming to increase his parliamentary support after lawmakers last week rejected proposals to address a housing crisis that has drawn nationwide protests. Speaking with FRANCE 24's Mark Owen, Javier Carbonell, Policy Analyst at the European Policy Centre, explains that Sanchez has chosen "the best moment in a sea of troubles" to call snap elections as he is likely to capitalise on the mobilisation of left-wing voters during the housing protests.</summary></entry><entry><title>Russian officials say 'situation under control' after plague reports</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f4ae666084121f452a0ba93a8824fe8b793431b90e3c999adacc8af1cd5421b5</id><updated>2026-10-06T06:35:16Z</updated><published>2026-10-05T19:19:10Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/russian-officials-say-situation-under-control-after-plague-reports--055d98c21474.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/russian-officials-say-situation-under-control-after-plague-reports" /><summary type="html">Moscow on Monday downplayed reports that a laboratory technician had died of plague, stressing that post-mortem tests had not detected the disease, while Washington said it was closely monitoring the situation. Reports on Friday that plague had killed a 28-year-old woman named Darya Shipilova, who had been working for the anti-plague institute in Siberia's Irkutsk region, sparked alarm. FRANCE 24's August Hakansson reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>Saudi-backed Yemeni forces expel the Houthis from several areas around key strait, officials say</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d756c4d7a9802f45202f2bf6cf4e85da9a271087385a17eeeae7345f18e6cd3c</id><updated>2026-10-06T06:35:19Z</updated><published>2026-10-05T19:17:05Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/saudi-backed-yemeni-forces-expel-the-houthis-from-several-areas-around-key-strait-officials-say--6def5d5b3087.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/saudi-backed-yemeni-forces-expel-the-houthis-from-several-areas-around-key-strait-officials-say" /><summary type="html">Saudi-backed Yemeni government forces staged a lightning advance on ​Monday to retake the coast around the Bab el-Mandeb Strait up to the city of Mocha, the government said, pushing the Iran-backed Houthis out of most of the areas they seized last month. FRANCE 24's Monte Francis reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>Return of the Bolsonaros: Why the far-right surge in Brazilian elections?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4fbaa61b19565bd3953800f4af0bf23852d906c961b007d29f0a017839805600</id><updated>2026-10-06T06:35:22Z</updated><published>2026-10-05T18:44:35Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20261005-return-of-the-bolsonaros-why-the-far-right-surge-in-brazilian-elections--907a05e0e477.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20261005-return-of-the-bolsonaros-why-the-far-right-surge-in-brazilian-elections" /><summary type="html">Do voters care about attempted coups? Brazil's Flavio Bolsonaro on the cusp of unseating Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva in the October 25th presidential runoff, Bolsonaro whose father was jailed over the Brazilian version of the January 6th storming of the US Capitol. Up and down the ballot, there are other Bolsonaros elected in the first round as the far-right surges. Is it about incumbent fatigue? Do Brazilians subscribe to Bolsonaro’s "God, Homeland, Family" mantra?</summary><category term="The Debate" /></entry><entry><title>France, Germany seek new EU rapid response tool against trade threats</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:275637b02c007c1edd710f5cc7960dff07f87b2955e0bec4ab330015e1688c02</id><updated>2026-10-06T06:33:30Z</updated><published>2026-10-05T17:01:26Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261005-france-germany-seek-new-eu-rapid-response-tool-against-trade-threats--a4fdd4599ffc.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261005-france-germany-seek-new-eu-rapid-response-tool-against-trade-threats" /><summary type="html">French President Emmanuel Macron and German Chancellor Friedrich Merz on Monday announced they would develop a new legal tool to enable the EU to respond rapidly to trade wars or measures, such as dumping. While they did not say the proposal was a direct response to the actions of any particular country, it came days before EU Chief Ursula von der Leyen visits China to tackle trade frictions.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>ICC unseals arrest warrants for Taliban education ministers</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d29ec79409c12d6252de916ccfa9cf96230a36a8d7b4c2012e7c9816e2cb2d9d</id><updated>2026-10-06T06:33:30Z</updated><published>2026-10-05T16:16:48Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261005-icc-unseals-arrest-warrants-for-taliban-education-ministers--eef86bb29f9a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261005-icc-unseals-arrest-warrants-for-taliban-education-ministers" /><summary type="html">The International Criminal Court on Monday unsealed warrants for Afghan Education Minister Habibullah Agha, and Higher Education Minister Neda Mohammad Nadeem, accusing two senior Taliban officials of crimes against humanity for denying Afghanistan's women and girls over 12 their rights to an education.</summary><category term="Asia / Pacific" /></entry><entry><title>Quebec separatists vow independence vote after provincial election win</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:278f4a3c3a84c835d033f32d9c31c5821fa4dc305af4bbdb891158d669894f11</id><updated>2026-10-06T06:35:25Z</updated><published>2026-10-05T16:08:47Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261005-separatists-win-quebec-election-with-pledge-to-vote-on-leaving-canada--1a6d962e8ede.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261005-separatists-win-quebec-election-with-pledge-to-vote-on-leaving-canada" /><summary type="html">The separatist Parti Québécois won provincial elections on Monday, but fell just short of enough seats to govern alone in Canada's French-speaking province, Quebec. The victory comes just two weeks ahead of a vote in Alberta, Canada's economic powerhouse, on whether it wants to begin the process of leaving the country.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>French high school students predict escalation of protests</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:da61948233378b3db2419d9a8016eca96fb4df88347cd89f4cbf52ac69f188dc</id><updated>2026-10-06T06:33:30Z</updated><published>2026-10-05T15:57:51Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261005-french-high-school-students-predict-escalation-of-protests--fde7355d8a27.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261005-french-high-school-students-predict-escalation-of-protests" /><summary type="html">Lessons were suspended at hundreds of French high schools on Monday, as part of a wave of student protests over learning conditions that have rocked the European nation. Larger demonstrations are expected on Tuesday.</summary></entry><entry><title>ISIS suspects face 'outsourced' justice in Iraq as HRW warns of 'collective global detention crisis'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:842e3da73111e1413e4f3222b108fc05ccc1f96bc4ed95004ceaca053d1db6b5</id><updated>2026-10-06T06:33:30Z</updated><published>2026-10-05T15:46:33Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261005-isis-suspects-face-outsourced-justice-in-iraq-as-hrw-warns-of-collective-global-detention-c--177d80f183d4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261005-isis-suspects-face-outsourced-justice-in-iraq-as-hrw-warns-of-collective-global-detention-crisis-1" /><summary type="html">Erin Ogunkeye is pleased to welcome Letta Tayler, Senior Counterterrorism Advisor at Human Rights Watch. She warns of the detention of suspected Islamic State members transferred from northeast Syria to Iraq as part of a much wider "global detention crisis". The men and boys now held in Iraq are living in 'dire' conditions, including deaths from illness, allegations of torture, and serious questions surrounding access to effective legal representation. Can accountability be achieved through legal proceedings that respect the rule of law and provide genuine justice to both detainees and victims?</summary></entry><entry><title>How Lula’s successes in Brazil may have paved the way for his presidential defeat</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:33e657132af04d85dc2499df3626dc75fc871d03699e7e7b4a7227e90c005956</id><updated>2026-10-06T06:33:30Z</updated><published>2026-10-05T15:21:10Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261005-how-lulas-successes-in-brazil-may-have-paved-the-way-for-his-presidential-defeat--860d2205f908.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261005-how-lulas-successes-in-brazil-may-have-paved-the-way-for-his-presidential-defeat" /><summary type="html">Brazil’s veteran leftist President Luiz Inacio "Lula" da Silva trailed Flavio Bolsonaro, the son of his far-right predecessor, in the first-round presidential vote on Sunday. Some analysts suggest that the sweeping anti-poverty measures Lula put in place over two decades may have helped give rise to a growing lower-middle class drawn to the far right’s promise to get the government out of people’s lives.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry></feed>
